achievement.announce.disenchanter_server_first.body = {0} pulled the server's first Disenchanter's Grimoire out of a table: {1}
achievement.announce.disenchanting_master.title = Master Disenchanter!
achievement.announce.disenchanting_orrins_own.title = Orrin's Own!

dialogue.mmo_enchanter.first_words.text = You are standing in my light. No matter. Stay.\nI am Orrin. I was a priest of the cult once, and the robes do not come off as easily as the belief did. Here in the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color> I keep a table that takes a piece of gear apart and gives back what went into it. Say your name and we will speak properly.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.first_words.opt.hail = Hello, Orrin.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.sent_by_sawyer.text = The sawyer sent you. He shouts, that one, and he is right more often than he knows.\nHe said you had the patience for a slow table. We shall see. Greet me properly and we will call you introduced.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.sent_by_sawyer.opt.hail = Hello, Orrin.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.menu.text = Orrin is listening. Speak, or go and feed the table; it does not mind which.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.trophy_hail.text = Wait. Let me see that.\nThe <color is="#ffd97a">Disenchanter's Grimoire</color>. A whole book, drawn out of a great many unmade things, and it fell to you. I have sat at that table for years and it has never once given me one.\nIt casts, and in your hand it hurries the rite along. Keep it shut when you sleep.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.trophy_hail.opt.show = It came out of the table.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.trophy_talk.text = You still carry the <color is="#ffd97a">Disenchanter's Grimoire</color>. Good. A book like that wants reading at the table. Do not let it sit on a shelf. What do you need?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.table_offer.text = I keep a frame for a <b>Disenchanting Table</b> and nothing to finish it with. The wood and the stone I have. The rest I do not.\nBring me <b>iron bars</b> and <b>life essence</b>, and I will build it and put it in your hands. It takes a piece of gear apart and gives back a share of what the forge put in, and a little more besides.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.table_offer.opt.accept = I will bring the iron and the essence.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.table_brief.text = <b>Iron bars</b> from a furnace and <b>life essence</b> from wherever you find it; the farms make it, and the sawyer's mill shakes it loose. Bring both and the table is yours.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.table_ready.text = <b>Iron</b>, and <b>essence</b>. Let me see them. Yes, this will do.\nThere. A Disenchanting Table, built around a frame I have kept longer than I care to say. Set it on level ground. The rest I will teach you.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.table_ready.opt.turnin = Here is the iron and the essence.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.unmaking_offer.text = Set the <b>table</b> down. Hold a <b>piece of gear</b>, use the table, and it takes the piece from your hand. Use it again and the rite begins.\nIt is slow. It is meant to be. Unmake a few pieces, and bring me a little of the <b>life essence</b> they give up, so I know the rite was done properly.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.unmaking_offer.opt.accept = I will unmake a few pieces.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.kinds_offer.text = A <b>sword</b> and a <b>breastplate</b> are not the same thing to the table, and a <b>hatchet</b> is a third thing again. Each gives back a share of what it was made of.\nUnmake some of each, and you will know what the table knows.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.kinds_offer.opt.accept = I will bring it some of each.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.kinds_offer.opt.what = What will the table take?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.draw_offer.text = <b>Life essence</b> is the wage of this work. Every piece gives up some; a better piece gives up more.\nDraw a proper measure of it out of gear, and bring me a share. I have uses for it that the alchemists do not.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.draw_offer.opt.accept = I will bring you essence.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.draw_ready.text = There. <b>Life essence</b>, still warm from the unmaking. Most who sit at the table pocket it and never think where it came from. Give it here.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.draw_ready.opt.turnin = Here is the essence.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.worn_offer.text = Gear that is nearly spent still holds something. You will learn less from a spent piece than from a fresh one, I will not pretend otherwise, but less is more than nothing.\nTake the <b>blades</b> you were about to throw away and the <b>boots</b> you walked through, and sit at the table until they are all gone.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.worn_offer.opt.accept = I will unmake what is worn.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.mithril_offer.text = <b>Mithril</b> is forged with void in it. Every smith knows and none of them say so.\nSet one <b>mithril piece</b> on the table and watch what comes out of it. You will not like how much went in.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.mithril_offer.opt.accept = I will unmake a mithril piece.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.mithril_ready.text = You saw it come apart, then. There is void in mithril, put there at the forge. When the piece is armor, some of that void comes off the table with the ore and the hide. A mithril weapon or tool gives back ore and hide and none of the void. Past that, the table finds a little void of its own now and then.\nNow you know what the smiths put in their steel. Sit a moment. This is the part most people walk away from.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.mithril_ready.opt.turnin = I saw it.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.hands_offer.text = The rite rewards a practised hand. The kit and the draught both hurry it, but nothing replaces sitting at the <b>table</b> until the work stops frightening you.\nSit there a long while, and let your craft grow to match it. There is nothing to bring me. I will know.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.hands_offer.opt.accept = I will put the hours in.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.greater_offer.text = There is a wider table. It holds three pieces at once and works them one after another, and it draws deeper than the one you have.\nIt wants <b>thorium bars</b> and <b>bolts of silk</b>, and <b>void essence</b> to wake it. Bring me those and I will build it around a frame I have kept a long time. The essence comes out of good gear; you have seen it.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.greater_offer.opt.accept = I will bring the makings.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.greater_brief.text = <b>Thorium</b> from the deep furnaces and <b>silk</b> from the loom, with <b>void essence</b> out of the table to wake it. Bring all of it. I will not build it from less.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.greater_ready.text = The <b>thorium</b> and the <b>silk</b>, and the <b>void</b> to wake it. Let me see them. Yes.\nThere. The Greater Disenchanting Table. Three sockets, left to right, and the rite walks through them without stopping. It finds void more often than the small one does. Set it somewhere with room.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.greater_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the makings.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.shadoweave_offer.text = The cult weaves a cloth that drinks the light. <b>Shadoweave</b>, they call it. I wore it for years and never once felt warm.\nBring me <b>scraps</b> of it off the Outlanders, and unmake the <b>weapons</b> they carry, and I will tell you why I left.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.shadoweave_offer.opt.accept = I will bring the scraps.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.shadoweave_offer.opt.why = Why did you leave?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.shadoweave_ready.text = <b>Shadoweave</b>. I had not held any in a long time. It is colder than I remembered.\nTheir weapons are unmade and the cloth is here. Give me the <b>scraps</b>, and I will keep my side of it.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.shadoweave_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the scraps.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.thread_offer.text = Good gear carries a thread of void in it, put there at the forge. The table pulls it loose, and the better the piece, the more it gives.\nDraw some <b>void essence</b> out of gear and bring me a few threads. I keep count of what I take back.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.thread_offer.opt.accept = I will draw out some void.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.thread_offer.opt.what = What is void, to you?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.steel_offer.text = The <b>Outlanders</b> carry <b>Doomed weapons</b>, forged with more void than any smith should use. I carried one. I know the weight.\nTake some from them. Then set the weapons on the table and let it drain them. That is the only cure I have found.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.steel_offer.opt.accept = I will bring their steel to the table.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.voidheart_offer.text = A <b>Voidheart</b> is the void given a shape. The deepest gear hides one now and then, and the void's own creatures carry them.\nWork the <b>greater table</b> until you are sure of it, then bring me one heart. I have a book to give you, and I do not give it lightly.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.voidheart_offer.opt.accept = I will bring you a Voidheart.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.voidheart_brief.text = The <b>greater table</b>, until your hands are sure. Then one <b>Voidheart</b>, from wherever you can find it. Take your time. The book has waited longer than you have.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.voidheart_ready.text = A <b>Voidheart</b>. Give it here. Yes. It is still beating, in its way.\nThis is my own grimoire, written before I left and rewritten since. It is a lesser book than the one the table gives out, and I know it. It casts, and in hand it hurries the rite and brings the table's finds round a little more often. <color is="#ffd97a">Orrin's Grimoire</color>, and there is no other. It is yours.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.voidheart_ready.opt.turnin = Here is the heart.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.iron_offer.text = The sawyer is always short of iron, and he does not like to say so.\nUnmake a few <b>iron hatchets</b> at the table; worn ones will do. The <b>iron ore</b> they give back, carry across the landing to <color is="#ffd97a">Sawyer Marn</color>. He will pay you for it, and I will not have to listen to him.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.iron_offer.opt.accept = I will carry the iron to Marn.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.second_offer.text = One table serves one pair of hands. You have more work than that.\nPut a great many pieces through yours, and bring me <b>life essence</b> from the work, and I will build you a second table.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.second_offer.opt.accept = I will put the pieces through.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.rites_ready.text = The day's rites, kept. The pieces are gone and the <b>essence</b> is here. That is all I ask. Take what I keep for you. Tomorrow, the same.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.rites_ready.opt.turnin = Here is the day's tithe.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.threads_ready.text = The order is filled. The armor and the weapons are unmade, and the <b>essence</b> is counted. Take what I pay out of it, and look in the pile for cloth. It comes round again before long.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.threads_ready.opt.turnin = Here is the tithe.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.week_ready.text = A week, and the <b>void essence</b> to show for it. The pieces are unmade, the essence drawn, and the void is back where it belongs. A week well spent, by my reckoning. Take your due.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.week_ready.opt.turnin = Here is the week's void.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.ready_generic.text = You have the look of somebody carrying a finished thing. Set it down and we will settle.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.ready_generic.opt.turnin = Here is what I have done.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.active_generic.text = Still at the work, then. The table does nothing without a hand on it. Go on.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.vow_talk.text = You carry my grimoire, and you have heard why I left. There is nothing of mine left to give you.\nThe table is another matter. It gives out a book of its own when it chooses, and it has never chosen me. Sit at it. There is work here when you want it, as there always was.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.greater_talk.text = The greater table is yours, and it draws deep. You have gone further at this than anyone I have taught.\nI have a story of my own, if you care to hear it, and the rites keep coming round. Ask.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.table_talk.text = You have a table now. Keep it fed. Every piece gives up its essence, and the better the piece, the more it gives. There is work here when you want it.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.how_it_works.text = Hold a <b>piece of gear</b> and use the <b>table</b>, and it takes the piece from your hand. Use it again and the rite begins: the book opens and the piece lifts, and when the power has built high enough the piece comes apart.\nWhat comes back is what the Salvager's Workbench would give, with life essence on top. Now and then there is more. Your Enchanting grows with every rite, and a practised hand works faster.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.how_it_works.opt.takes = What will it take?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.how_it_works.opt.back = I understand.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.what_it_takes.text = <b>Weapons</b> and <b>armor</b>, and the <b>tools</b> you work with. A shield counts as a weapon to the table. Anything a forge or a loom made to be worn or swung.\nIt will not take ammunition or bait, and it will not take its own grimoire or the kit it pays out. A spent piece teaches you less and a stamped piece more. One piece at a time, on the small table.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.what_it_takes.opt.bench = And the Salvager's Workbench?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.what_it_takes.opt.back = Good to know.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.the_bench.text = The Salvager's Workbench takes a piece apart in a breath and gives you a share of what went in. Nothing more. It does not care who stands at it.\nMy table takes its time. It gives back the same share, then the essence, and whatever else the piece was hiding. It cares a great deal who stands at it. Use the bench when you are in a hurry. Use the table when you want to learn.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.the_bench.opt.back = I see the difference.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.the_greater_how.text = The <b>greater table</b> has three sockets, left to right. Hold a piece, use the table, and it fills the next empty one. Fill all three if you like.\nUse it again and the rite walks through them, one after another, with no pause between. It draws more essence from each piece than the small one does, and it finds void more often. It takes longer.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.the_greater_how.opt.back = Three at a time, then.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.what_is_void.text = The void is what is left when something is unmade and nothing is given back. The cult worships that. I did, once.\nThe forge puts a thread of it into mithril and into the Doomed steel, and the table draws the thread back out as void essence. A Voidheart is the same thing, grown large enough to hold a shape. The alchemists want both. So do I, though not for the same reasons.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.what_is_void.opt.back = I will remember that.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.grimoire_tease.text = There is a book. The <color is="#ffd97a">Disenchanter's Grimoire</color>. The table gives it out when it chooses, drawn whole out of a great many unmade things, and it chooses rarely.\nIt casts, and in the hand it hurries the rite along. I have sat at that table for years. It has never chosen me.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.grimoire_tease.opt.back = I will keep unmaking.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.kit_talk.text = There is a kit. Silk, from the <b>hood</b> down to the <b>leggings</b>, and the robe comes up least of all. The table pays it out a piece at a time, when it chooses, and I pay a piece now and then out of the <b>loose threads</b>.\nWear it and the rite goes faster. Wear the whole of it with the grimoire in hand and it goes faster still.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.kit_talk.opt.back = I will watch for it.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.why_i_left.text = The cult taught that the void is holy, and that a thing unmade is a thing freed. I believed it. I unmade a great many things.\nThen I watched a brother of mine unmake a village and call it freedom. I walked out that night with the robes on my back and this book under my arm, and I have been drawing the void back out of things ever since. It is slow work. It is the only work I know.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.why_i_left.opt.void = And the void itself?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.why_i_left.opt.back = Thank you for telling me.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.returned = I have come back with what you asked for.
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.quests = Anything to unmake?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.how = How does the table work?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.takes = What will the table take?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.bench = What about the Salvager's Workbench?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.greater = How does the greater table work?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.grimoire = Does the table give anything rare?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.kit = Where does the kit come from?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.why = Why did you leave the cult?
dialogue.mmo_enchanter.opt.nothing = Nothing for now.

